                },
                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "40800281",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198136868737",
                            "num_reviews": 64,
                            "playtime_forever": 68,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 68,
                            "last_played": 1520993405
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This is an excellent game for some friends to gather around and play together. My only complaint was that the screen shook wildly whenever a ship exploded, however, the developer actually took the time to answer my comment on the game's discussion board: within a very short amount of time a slider bar for explosion shake was added!\n\nIn this game you (and either AI or friends) build a modular ship and then engage in battle. Unless you're playing sandbox mode (which is crazy) you will have a limited amount of \"component cards\" to choose from after each round. For instance, in the start you can build, say, 4 parts onto your ship. The current \"cards\" may be (2) thrusters, (1) minigun and (1) armor. When you use one to add to your ship, the \"card\" slot is filled with another random card. You do this until you use up the allowed 4 or until you're finished. This is repeated after each round. \n\nIf you lose your ship, you have to restart from the base of your ship. If you survive then you get to continue building on your ship or start a new one. It might sound brutal but the rounds are very quick so it's not like you lose a lot of hard work.\n\nTry it out for yourself, especially if it is on sale!",
                        "timestamp_created": 1520994073,
